00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.490 align:start position:0%
rust can be a little bit confusing when  you first get started this is an open  world survival game with no real goal  other than staying alive and considering  that you start out with nothing more  than bandages a torch and a big old rock  it's pretty easy to feel lost literally  and figuratively here are a few tips to  help tip the odds of survival in your  favor the first thing you need to do is  build yourself a hatchet you do this by  collecting pieces of wood and a few  stones what is the easy part  find any old tree and smash it with your  router  your inventory will automatically fill  up with the wood stones are a little bit  trickier you'd think that you could just  bash those rocky cliffs all around the  map but nope you need to find these  respawning boulders out in the middle of  fields smash away at a few of these with  old rocky and you should have enough  stones to get the job done now open your  crafting screen select stone hatchet and  assemble away congratulations and you  just made surviving slightly easier the  hatchet is useful because not only does  it make harvesting wood that much faster  it's also a much more reliable weapon  than the rock you start out with this is  important for your next objective and  rust which is to gather some food before  you starve to death your best bet is to  find a wild animal like a boar sneak up  to it and hatch it away now this next  part is important that raw meat you just  dropped through killing animals for the  love of God make sure to cook it on a  campfire eat it raw and you're in for a  world of hurt  virtual Salmonella is no one's friend  trust me on that one I've made that  mistake before now that you've got food  in a weapon you should focus on creating  shelter a simple Shack will do the trick  and building a wooden door to go with it  will keep you safe from animals zombies  and any player who doesn't have the  patience to hack away with it with a  hatchet just make sure to place your  shelter in a relatively low traffic area  like up in the hills or near the water  at the edge of the map anyone with  enough time and resources can break into  your shelter but tucking it away  somewhere quiet will help reduce the  chances of burglar  now find some cloth from dead animal and  build yourself a sleeping bag so that  you'll have a respawn point the next  time you die or log back into the server  oh and if you're in a sleeper server  that means that your body falls limp to  the ground when you log off so make sure  you log off inside of your shelter if  you don't want to get murdered in your  sleep with shelter taken care of you  should work on crafting yourself some  more advanced weapons something like the  bow and arrow a bow requires wood and  cloth while arrows require wood and  stone the bow and arrow is nice for  general defence against hostile players  but it's especially nice for hunting  zombies the undead do a lot of damage at  close range so taking them out from afar  is critical hunting zombies is a good  use of time because they tend to drop  really high-value items that you can't  craft on your own or at least not as a  beginner and finally a little advice for  getting around there's no in-game map so  if you want to know where you are you're  gonna need to cheat a little bit so  here's what you do hit shift tab to pull  open the steam overlay open up the web  browser and go to rust map dotnet you  can also just alt tab this if you want  now this map is a great way to  familiarize yourself with the games  primary landmarks so that you can have  an easier time getting around you'll  probably still get lost but at least  you'll be doing it less often than  before and with that you should be set  all that's left is learning how to deal  with other players hold via to use voice  chat so that you could tell them you're  friendly and hopefully they don't kill  you on sight just be careful around  players with fancy armor and those who  are building giant houses they're the  ones with the most to lose and as a  result they tend to be the most  offensive so just be friendly and you  should hopefully be fine excuse me sir  good luck and have fun out there for  more rust coverage make sure to go to  GameSpot calm  the trick
 

